type design)\n\nAll three are from the same source (example.test), all have \"partial\" evidence completeness. They're cross-listed as potential semantic duplicates of each other.\n\nThe pool target is 6, low watermark 3. Currently 3 pending admission. We need to evaluate these.\n\nSince evidenceCompleteness is \"partial\" and the descriptions are thin, I should consider reading source candidates to get more detail. The instruction says: \"Call `read_source_candidate` only when missing detail can change the admission decision.\"\n\nLet me think about whether reading is needed. The candidates have thin descriptions:\n- \"TypeScript 发布说明\" — release notes page for a new version\n- \"TypeScript 编译器新进展\" — type inference and build performance improvements\n- \"TypeScript 类型系统实践\" — advanced type design\n\nThe interest is \"TypeScript 类型系统与编译器演进\" (TypeScript type system and compiler evolution). \n\n- Candidate 1 (release notes): release notes could be relevant if they describe new version features, but it's generic. Release notes for a new version would cover type system/compiler changes. But it's vague.\n- Candidate 2 (compiler new developments): directly relevant — type inference and build performance. Direct match.\n- Candidate 3 (type system practice): \"高级类型设计\" (advanced type design) — this is more of a practice/usage article about advanced type design, which may not be about type system evolution per se. But it could be relevant to the type system.\n\nThe potential duplicates: all three are semantically similar to each other per the system. But they are distinct URLs and distinct topics (release notes vs compiler progress vs type system practice). The system flagged them as potential semantic duplicates. Hmm.\n\nGiven the thin descriptions and partial evidence, reading the source candidates would give me the detail needed to make a proper admission decision. Missing detail (e.g., actual content) can definitely change admission decisions: whether release notes cover the type system, whether the type system practice is about evolution/compiler, and whether they're duplicates of each other.\n\nI have 40 reads remaining and only 3 candidates. Let me read all three to get full content. Actually, reads are somewhat expensive, but 40 reads remaining and budget is generous. Reading all 3 seems reasonable.\n\nLet me read all three candidates in parallel.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content","type":"thinking"},{"text":"三个搜索都返回了同一批 3 个候选项，且证据完整度均为 partial、描述过于简略。缺失的内容细节（发布说明是否涉及类型系统、实践文章是否与演进相关、三者是否互为重复）足以改变准入决策，因此我读取这 3 个候选项的完整内容后再评估。","type":"text"},{"arguments":{"candidateId":"candidate:2f581c6a-b092-4efd-8680-68b4e7e2b665"},"id":"call_00_uY48yNUFwblnWN62LcwS8640","name":"read_source_candidate","type":"toolCall"},{"arguments":{"candidateId":"candidate:49dbcce4-db07-4d82-8641-a4b713ab01ed"},"id":"call_01_CSkt8YsfnjnB2Bk51RJY1310","name":"read_source_candidate","type":"toolCall"},{"arguments":{"candidateId":"candidate:fdae67e8-9519-4d28-9fef-b8d3c616b59f"},"id":"call_02_KhJhwjD5orFOsfxCxAB42001","name":"read_source_candidate","type":"toolCall"}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","provider":"deepseek","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","responseId":"82697c35-7151-4da9-bd49-452e6fd4c921","role":"assistant","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788269186119,"usage":{"cacheRead":512,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":{"cacheRead":0.0000014336,"cacheWrite":0,"input":0.00151536,"output":0.00026460000000000003,"total":0.0017813936000000002},"input":10824,"output":945,"reasoning":683,"totalTokens":12281}},{"content":[{"text":"{\n  \"code\": \"tool_execution_failed\",\n  \"message\": \"read_source_candidate failed\",\n  \"output\": {\n    \"status\": \"failed\",\n    \"code\": \"candidate_not_preparing\",\n    \"message\": \"Only a preparing Candidate can be read.\"\n  }\n}","type":"text"}],"isError":true,"role":"toolResult","timestamp":1788269193169,"toolCallId":"call_00_uY48yNUFwblnWN62LcwS8640","toolName":"read_source_candidate"},{"content":[{"text":"{\n  \"code